g to Himmelman (1992), what role should communities play to achieve real empowerment?','medium','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(57,1,'What is the first step in the 5 Steps of Community Organizing?','hard','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(58,1,'What is a key characteristic of the Centralized Specialty Care model?','medium','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(59,1,'Decentralized Health Care Services aim to:','medium','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(60,1,'Which of the following is an effect of health on a community?','easy','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(61,2,'How is \"Behavior\" generally defined in the context of this lecture?','medium','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(62,2,'Which classification of behavior is described as \"occurring without thinking\" or an unconscious reflex action?','easy','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(63,2,'Which classification refers to actions that are done with reason and conscious awareness?','easy','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(64,2,'A person thinking or breathing is an example of which type of behavior?','medium','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(65,2,'An observable behavior, such as walking or talking, is classified as:','easy','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(66,2,'Behavior that is done consciously and within a person\'s control is called:','medium','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(67,2,'Which viewpoint on human behavior believes that the mind dominates most bodily activities?','medium','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(68,2,'According to the Biological Viewpoint, everything you think and feel is controlled by:','easy','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(69,2,'Which viewpoint focuses on how people interact with others and how their environment influences their actions?','medium','2026-09-05 16:33:01','2026-09-05 16:33:01'),(70,2,'Which part of a neuron is considered the